\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The one-variable test (rung sequence as above), shown per held-out \emph  {eval contrast} rather than pooled, one panel per dataset, grouped by boundary type. Each line is one (training modality, eval contrast) pair across all seven rungs; colour is the fill-swap step's own significance (Holm-corrected paired Wilcoxon within that ladder's own contrast family): teal = significant improvement, red = significant worsening, grey = not significant. Solid/dashed = trained on a T1-weighted vs.\ T2-weighted/FLAIR contrast; marker shape = eval contrast, one mapping reused across every panel. No-tissue-interface tasks (BraTS-GLI, Open-MS): 8 of 10 curves improve significantly at the fill swap, 1 worsens significantly (BraTS-GLI T2w$\to $T1n, discussed below), 1 is flat. Tissue-interface tasks (CHAOS, ON-Harmony): only 1 of 16 improves and 1 worsens significantly -- the step is a non-event for 14 of 16 (88\%). Dice numbers pooled per ladder in \cref  {tab:dissociation}; HD95 in \cref  {sec:suppl-persetting}.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{2}{8}{The one-variable test (rung sequence as above), shown per held-out \emph {eval contrast} rather than pooled, one panel per dataset, grouped by boundary type. Each line is one (training modality, eval contrast) pair across all seven rungs; colour is the fill-swap step's own significance (Holm-corrected paired Wilcoxon within that ladder's own contrast family): teal = significant improvement, red = significant worsening, grey = not significant. Solid/dashed = trained on a T1-weighted vs.\ T2-weighted/FLAIR contrast; marker shape = eval contrast, one mapping reused across every panel. No-tissue-interface tasks (BraTS-GLI, Open-MS): 8 of 10 curves improve significantly at the fill swap, 1 worsens significantly (BraTS-GLI T2w$\to $T1n, discussed below), 1 is flat. Tissue-interface tasks (CHAOS, ON-Harmony): only 1 of 16 improves and 1 worsens significantly -- the step is a non-event for 14 of 16 (88\%). Dice numbers pooled per ladder in \cref {tab:dissociation}; HD95 in \cref {sec:suppl-persetting}.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{fig:ladder@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][7][]8}}
